From fd72a94bb4ff34b6e6033fa5d8cb48dda55dce20 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ws07 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:18:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ws07: arrival wording matched to 04's contract; misdelivered
 and unread states
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- A village's recorded intake is its lower bound: each resource "n 以上", all
  zero "0 以上" (never "なし"); the units line says why (cargo_log drops under one).
- A storehouse: "到着しましたが、入った量は確認できません（最大 n）" — arrived, the
  intake unknown, at most the record (settle_caravan cuts at the cap).
- Settled at another place than the send named with no take read: new state
  `misdelivered`, "別の場所に着きました（原因を確認中）"; no raid named and nothing
  counted. A take read after the send (`sent.taken`) keeps the raider's
  intake-only state, whose text no longer gives a raid as an example.
- A caravan that leaves the road's list while the page watches, with no end
  read: new state `unread` ("状態不明"), cleared when the away reader reads its
  settlement or raid; memory only, so a reload says nothing of it.
- Overdue says "読み込んだ時点では" (what was read, not the world).
- English words; tests: contracts, connect (misdelivered, taken, unread,
  reload), away (entry line after "seen" and a reload), harness screen rows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C5Nj2bNLFpFghsNM9fsQG5
